Figure 7: Coma surface-brightness profile of C/2011 L3 from the light added to 12 772 faint stars in Q10, as a
function of each star’s distance from the predicted nucleus. Red: power-law fit $S\propto\rho^{-1.21}$; blue:
$\rho^{-1}$.

Figure 7: Angular resolution as a function of the track energy, expressed as the $\sigma$ of the narrower gaussian component (yellow) and of the broader gaussian component (purple), with the corresponding fit functions superimposed. In green also the fraction of events falling within the narrower gaussian over the sum of events falling in the two gaussians is shown. The curves are extended beyond the fitted energy interval
to illustrate the extrapolation of the empirical parametrization;
these regions are not constrained by the simulated data.
